Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2C): deduplicate near-identical
closed gap-fill loops + emit closed gap-fill as a single
ExtrusionLoop with average width.

Why: the variable-width / medial-axis gap-fill solver can emit
near-duplicate closed loops when thin features produce overlapping
ThickPolylines. The existing code emits both; the printer prints
the same loop twice and surface quality degrades (over-extrusion
ridges, slight glossiness change).

Adds three new helpers:
  - `closed_loop_points` strips the duplicate first/last vertex
    closing the loop so cyclic comparison works.
  - `points_match_cyclic` compares two equal-size vertex lists with
    arbitrary rotation and either winding direction, tolerance
    `scale_(0.05)` mm per vertex.
  - `are_near_duplicate_closed_gap_fill_loops` is the predicate:
    bbox match, total-length match (±0.20 mm), absolute-area match
    (±0.05 mm × max-length), then the cyclic vertex match in
    either direction.
  - `closed_gap_fill_loop_to_extrusion_paths` builds a single
    ExtrusionPath at the length-weighted average width — replaces
    the segment-soup the default path would produce.

`variable_width()` itself runs the dedup pass only for `erGapFill`
with >1 input polyline (the cost is O(n²) on polyline count, fine
for the typical gap-fill set size of <100). For closed polylines
it prefers the new single-path-at-average-width emission, falling
back to the existing thick_polyline_to_extrusion_paths_2 split if
the closed-loop path returns empty (degenerate input).

Mechanical port from FS v0.9.9
(`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit b3c41fda),
`src/libslic3r/VariableWidth.cpp` lines 1-119 (helpers) + 331-360
(variable_width integration). This is a print-quality improvement
that ships independently of mixed-filament work; no behavior
change for non-gap-fill prints. Companion to patches 0029 + 0030.

